# Template for deploying cloudflared (Cloudflare Tunnel) on lab53.
# Copy to `.env` (NOT committed, see .gitignore) and fill in real values.
# Full reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-networks/

## Image version is pinned directly in docker-compose.yml (not here) so Renovate can
## track and bump it — see the note in CLAUDE.md about deploy-only Renovate coverage.

## Token for this tunnel, generated in the Zero Trust dashboard
## (Networks > Tunnels > create a tunnel > Docker installer). Copy just the token value
## shown there, not the whole install command.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=changeme

## Public Hostname rules (which hostname routes to which internal service, e.g.
## n8n.example.com -> http://lab56.local:5678) are configured in the same dashboard,
## not here — cloudflared just needs LAN reachability to the target Pi's hostname,
## which it has by default on the bridge network.
